    "body": "A worker on the Antino project site. Credit. Founders Metals.\nBy: Northern Miner Staff November 26, 2026\nFounders Metals (TSXV: FDR; US-OTC: FDMIF) has extended high-grade gold mineralization deeper at its Antino project in Suriname, where further drilling could help establish the scale of the Froyo zone.\nHole FR298 cut 15 metres grading 23.97 grams gold per tonne from 5094 metres downhole, Founders said Wednesday in a statement. The intercept extended the zone roughly 70 metres down its slope from a previously reported hole, the company said.\nLocated about 275 km southeast of Paramaribo, Suriname’s capital, Antino covers about 1,024 sq. km. A private airstrip and barges on the Lawa River give crews year-round access. The company gained full ownership of the property in September by acquiring the 30% stake it didn’t own. It also closed a $77-million (US$54 million) investment that raised Gold Fields’ (NYSE, JSE: GFI) stake in Founders to about 19.9%.\n“Antino is one of the best, and largest, exploration projects in the Guiana Shield, which Founders is positioned to systematically explore with the strategic backing of Gold Fields (…) and the recent consolidation of 100% ownership,” ATB Cormark mining analyst Nicolas Dion said Thursday in a note.\nPending assays\nWith the project’s deepest drilling to date now complete, “the next set of results will provide further insight into the scale of the mineralized system,” president and CEO Colin Padget said. Assays are pending from three subsequent deep holes.\nThe latest intercept extended the Froyo zone about 70 metres down its slope from hole FR230, which returned 9 metres at 12.21 grams gold per tonne in results announced June 23. The zone remains open at depth, and assays are pending from three subsequent deep holes. One of those, FR308, reached 884 metres downhole, the deepest hole yet at Upper Antino.\n“We see a high-grade, multi-million-ounce project emerging at the most advanced target (Upper Antino), while the rest of the Antino property hosts the potential for separate discoveries,” Dion said.\nFounders shares dropped 0.4% to $6.82 Thursday morning on the TSX Venture Exchange, valuing the Vancouver-based explorer at about C$982 million. They jumped 21% Wednesday after the drill results were released.\nPrint\nTAG: gold exploration gold projects\nCOMMODITY: Gold\nREGION: Canada South America\nCOMPANY: Founders Metals Gold Fields\nRepublish this article",
